# No server keys are needed: each visitor pastes their own provider key in the
# browser. It stays in sessionStorage and is sent only as a request header.
#
# Behind an HTTPS proxy (some corporate or cloud networks), Node's fetch ignores
# HTTPS_PROXY unless you start the app with NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1, e.g.
#   NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 npm run dev
